   <!-- Expected values, worked from the state's own form -->
   <!-- Sources: Oklahoma 2025 Form 511 packet: line 10 standard deduction, line 11 $1,000 per exemption, line 13 taxable income, line 14 Income Tax Table (bands 'at least X but less than X+50') and the $100,000-or-more computation on page 38. -->
   <!-- Federal: AGI $85,000; taxable $85,000 - $31,500 = $53,500 -->
   <!-- Oklahoma: line 10 $12,700; line 11 4 exemptions (two spouses, two
        dependents) x $1,000 = $4,000; line 13 $85,000 - $16,700 = $68,300.
        Table row at least $68,300 but less than $68,350, married filing
        joint: $2,868 (bracket tax at the $68,325 midpoint: $307 + 4.75% x
        $53,925 = $2,868.44) -->
